# Everything under runs/ is a per-run artefact -- .npz, .log, .msh, consoles, web exports,
# cluster .launch stamps and report .json. The extension list above already caught most of
# it, which is worse than catching none: `git add -A` would have committed the handful it
# missed (runs/*.launch, runs/cluster_report.json) and made the repo look like run output
# belongs in it. Ignore the directory and be done. Nothing here is tracked.
runs/

# The method paper. 30 MB, and not ours to redistribute -- keep it local, cite it in README.
refs/
